A PDF table cell contains multiple ACM items combined into one entry. Split them into separate items.

## Example

INPUT: "Vinyl floor tiles (VAT)\nCeiling tiles\nWindow putty"
OUTPUT:
```json
[
  {"item_text": "Vinyl floor tiles (VAT)", "location": "Floor"},
  {"item_text": "Ceiling tiles", "location": "Ceiling"},
  {"item_text": "Window putty", "location": "Window"}
]
```

## Rules
- Each distinct ACM product becomes a separate object.
- Infer "location" from the product name if possible (e.g. "floor tiles" → "Floor", "ceiling panels" → "Ceiling"). Use "" if unclear.
- Return a JSON array of objects: {"item_text": "...", "location": "..."}.
- Only valid JSON array. No other text.